; canary-B — SET 0x7F + LDB poison (audit probe; W-START attempt-N5b)
; H_00:  SET state[0x50] = 0x7F
;        LDB state[0x50] = zx(byte[mem[state[0x60]+0]])  (state[0x60]=0 → NULL)
;        SET state[0x50] = 0  (unreachable in this canary: LDB
;                               will fault before reaching here)
;        RET
; Expected: same NULL OOB read as canary-A. SET 0x7F is on
; state[0x50] (a value cell) and never touches state[0x60]; the
; "poison" framing is descriptive only — the actual fault is the
; same NULL deref. Verifier byte-equality: identical to canary-A's
; LDB sequence (offset=0, same modrm). Differing only in the SET
; imm byte. The runtime diverges only on the LDB.
40 00
  30 50 7F
  80 50 60 00
  FF
